i.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sureshanaparti","id":12028987,"login":"sureshanaparti","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti"}],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"### problem\n\nWindows guest instances (Virtual Desktops) do not find any Audio hardware.\n\n<img width=\"351\" height=\"158\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/350cc7cf-e758-497e-8615-c0851773fd17\" />\n\nBy adding `sound` to the global setting `allow.additional.vm.configuration.list.kvm`...\n\n<img width=\"1390\" height=\"124\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f7430d0d-d65f-4719-8ab4-c69579b7af11\" />\n\n...CloudMonkey can add this `extraconfig`.\n\n<img width=\"1009\" height=\"106\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2eeb6821-69ed-4b9c-b5e7-fbeeb37aba95\" />\n\n<img width=\"515\" height=\"436\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a1f42fad-9a33-46db-b6c5-bb2237693cf5\" />\n\nThen, after power cycling the VM, the issue is resolved.\n\n<img width=\"254\" height=\"121\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/606a92e2-3a94-43c2-a3d4-2c7d9e858f9a\" />\n\nIt does not feel like a feature request, but a \"bug\" to the default global settings.","comments":8,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889/comments","created_at":"2026-03-25T16:35:42Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889","id":4136813241,"labels":[{"color":"84b6eb","default":false,"description":"","id":37843366,"name":"type:enhancement","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:enhancement"},{"color":"006b75","default":false,"description":"","id":584072971,"name":"component:kvm","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzI5NzE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:kvm"},{"color":"ea62a8","default":false,"description":"","id":739374767,"name":"component:UI","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzkzNzQ3Njc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:UI"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":79,"created_at":"2026-01-21T11:18:05Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DaanHoogland","id":2486961,"login":"DaanHoogland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/45","id":14595362,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/45/labels","node_id":"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A3rUi","number":45,"open_issues":135,"state":"open","title":"4.20.4","updated_at":"2026-09-15T19:56:19Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/45"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M72ksK5","number":12889,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"Windows Guest Instances Have No Sound","updated_at":"2026-08-14T14:00:22Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12889","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90287660?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/daviftorres","id":90287660,"login":"daviftorres","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwMjg3NjYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daviftorres"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"### problem\n\n## Description\nWhen restoring a volume from backup and attaching it to a **running** KVM VM, the volume is only attached at the **database level** but not actually hot-attached to the running VM via libvirt. This means:\n1. The volume appears in CloudStack UI as \"attached\"\n2. The volume does NOT appear in `virsh domblklist <vm-name>` \n3. The volume is NOT visible inside the guest OS\n4. User must reboot(forced) the VM to see the restored volume\n## Root Cause\nIn `KVMGuru.attachRestoredVolumeToVirtualMachine()` (line 380-400), the method only:\n- Updates the volume state in the database via `_volumeDao.attachVolume()`\n- Sets volume state to `Ready`\nIt does **NOT**:\n- Check if VM is running\n- Send an `AttachCommand` to the KVM agent to hot-attach the disk via libvirt\n## Expected Behavior\nWhen attaching a restored volume to a **running** VM:\n1. CloudStack should detect the VM state\n2. If VM is [Running](cci:1://file:///root/new_merge/olympos-cloud-platform/plugins/hypervisors/kvm/src/main/java/com/cloud/hypervisor/kvm/resource/LibvirtComputingResource.java:5982:4-5991:5), send a libvirt attach command to hot-attach the disk\n3. Volume should immediately appear in `virsh domblklist` and inside guest OS\n4. No reboot should be required\n\n### versions\n\nCloudStack: 4.21.0\nHypervisor: KVM\nHost OS: Rocky Linux 9\nGuest OS: Rocky Linux 9 / Windows 10 - 2022 Server\n\n\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n1. Create a VM with a data disk\n2. Create a backup of the VM\n3. Start the VM (ensure it's running)\n4. Restore the backed-up volume and attach to the running VM via API:\n   `restoreVolumeFromBackupAndAttachToVM`\n5. Check `virsh domblklist <vm-name>` on the KVM host\n6. **Observe:** The restored volume is NOT listed\n7. Check inside guest OS\n8. **Observe:** The disk is NOT visible\n9. Reboot(forced) the VM\n10. **Observe:** After reboot(forced), the disk appears\n\n### What to do about it?\n\nEither:\nA) Add hot-attach logic to `KVMGuru.attachRestoredVolumeToVirtualMachine()` to send `AttachCommand` when VM is running\nB) Or document this as expected behavior and require users to stop VM before restoring volumes\nOption A is preferred as it aligns with how regular [attachVolume](cci:1://file:///root/new_merge/olympos-cloud-platform/server/src/main/java/com/cloud/storage/VolumeApiServiceImpl.java:2479:4-2483:5) API works for running VMs.","comments":3,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405/comments","created_at":"2026-01-12T11:28:53Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405","id":3803910012,"labels":[{"color":"4e62fc","default":false,"description":"","id":1155016910,"name":"status:needs-reproducing","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTU1MDE2OTEw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:needs-reproducing"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":114,"created_at":"2026-04-13T07:02:43Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12028987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sureshanaparti","id":12028987,"login":"sureshanaparti","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti"},"description":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/46","id":15514689,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46/labels","node_id":"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A7LxB","number":46,"open_issues":252,"state":"open","title":"4.22.2","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:13:59Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M7iuw98","number":12405,"reactions":{"+1":2,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":1,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":3,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"[KVM] Restored backup volume not attached to running VM via libvirt - only database updated","type":{"color":"red","created_at":"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z","description":"An unexpected problem or behavior","id":93570,"name":"Bug","node_id":"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFtgg","updated_at":"2024-07-26T10:04:57Z"},"updated_at":"2026-04-24T11:51:32Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/12405","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69652349?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/furkandogmus","id":69652349,"login":"furkandogmus","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NjUyMzQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/furkandogmus"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"<!--\r\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n<!-- Pick one below and delete the rest -->\r\n * Other / Question\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n<!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n-->\r\n~~~\r\nNetwork\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n<!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n~~~\r\nCloudStack 4.18.1.0\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n<!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n-->\r\n~~~\r\nNetwork in advanced core zone\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n<!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n-->\r\n~~~\r\nN/A\r\n~~~\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n<!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly -->\r\nCan you tell me if it is possible to add ipv6 to a deployed Shared network in an advanced core zone if the fields related to ipv6 were not filled in during its creation. Perhaps this can be achieved by editing the database? The important point is that there are already deployed vms in the network and their operability should not be disturbed. \r\n","comments":11,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8294/comments","created_at":"2023-12-01T13:51:35Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8294/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/8294","id":2020923395,"labels":[{"color":"cc317c","default":false,"description":"","id":37843368,"name":"type:question","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:question"},{"color":"c2e0c6","default":false,"description":"","id":584073336,"name":"component:ipv6","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzMzMzY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:ipv6"},{"color":"a5f9ff",