duyquy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leduyquy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leduyquy"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"<!--\r\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n<!-- Pick one below and delete the rest -->\r\n * Bug Report\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n<!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n-->\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n<!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n4.18\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n<!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n-->\r\n\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n<!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n-->\r\n\r\nubuntu 22.04.5\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n<!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly -->\r\n\r\nI have created an lxc instance【OS：centos 7】 and it appears to have started normally from the system. I used virsh -c lxc:///list on the host to check that lxc is also running. However, when I used virsh -c lxc:///console i-2-3-VM to enter the container instance, I was unable to use it properly. The prompt message is: Failed to create symlink/sys/fs/cgroup/net_cls: Operation not allowed; Did I not set it up properly somewhere;\r\n\r\n2、\r\nI logged into the virtual router and pinged the lxc instance's IP address in the virtual router, but it still doesn't work\r\n<img width=\"848\" alt=\"1732872762143\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5268116a-6e88-4906-be66-fe1eda50cd65\">\r\n\r\n<img width=\"509\" alt=\"1732873018388\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/62ad7246-6d8d-4d71-b934-ff6daab9b29f\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<img width=\"496\" alt=\"1732872892384\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dbfd50b5-1a6b-44b3-9b34-6cc7b0860289\">\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n<!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below -->\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n<!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files -->\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n<!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? -->\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n<!-- What actually happened? -->\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below -->\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":6,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011/comments","created_at":"2024-11-29T09:39:45Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011","id":2704557148,"labels":[{"color":"fc2929","default":false,"description":"","id":37843364,"name":"type:bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:bug"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":1302,"created_at":"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DaanHoogland","id":2486961,"login":"DaanHoogland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19","id":6265435,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels","node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==","number":19,"open_issues":185,"state":"open","title":"unplanned","updated_at":"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M6hNERc","number":10011,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"The lxc instance cannot connect","updated_at":"2026-09-17T13:36:00Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/10011","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/468252?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/maic","id":468252,"login":"maic","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2ODI1Mg==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maic"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"### problem\n\nHi.\nIn a advanced netowrk zone, VXLAN based, my KVM agents are using the storage network address as private ip address.\n\nThe network storage network is not routable between components, and it is causing severe problems like mal function on CPVM that try to connect on the wrong address to establish a connection with the hypervisor VNC Port.\n\nThe storage address is correctly found.\n\nThis is an exemple of my interfaces config:\n\n```\nroot@hypr2-rck3:~# ip -br a\nlo               UNKNOWN        127.0.0.1/8 10.1.4.2/32 fd00:1337:1:4::2/128 ::1/128 \nens8f0np0        DOWN           \nens8f1np1        DOWN           \nens5f0np0        UP             10.1.32.3/31 fd00:1337:1:20::3/127 fe80::e4f8:1110:2c37:62ca/64 \nens5f1np1        DOWN           \nvxlan200         UNKNOWN        \nvxlan202         UNKNOWN        \nv-secstorbr@v-secstor UP             \nv-secstor@v-secstorbr UP             10.1.48.2/22 fd00:1337:1:2d::2/64 fe80::a6c6:ac43:1c4:ab35/64 \nv-clmgmtbr@v-clmgmt UP             \nv-clmgmt@v-clmgmtbr UP             10.1.0.2/22 fd00:1337:1::2/64 fe80::a535:f84c:40f1:b424/64 \neth-clguest      UNKNOWN        \nv-clstoragebr@v-clstorage UP             \nv-clstorage@v-clstoragebr UP             10.1.16.2/20 fd00:1337:1:10::2/64 fe80::e263:1ef4:9243:237e/64 \nbr-secstor       UP             \neth-clpublic     UNKNOWN        \nvxlan100         UNKNOWN        \nbr-clmgmt        UP             \nbr-clguest       UP             \nbr-clstorage     UP             \nbr-clpublic      UP             \ncloud0           UNKNOWN        169.254.0.1/16 fe80::d028:d0ff:fe30:3c0d/64\n```\n\n\nagent.properties\n```\nroot@hypr2-rck3:~# cat /etc/cloudstack/agent/agent.properties\n#Storage\n#Tue Jun 30 18:10:35 BRT 2026\nLibvirtComputingResource.id=6\nLibvirtComputingResource.name=hypr2-rck3\nLibvirtComputingResource.uuid=***\ncluster=1\ndomr.scripts.dir=scripts/network/domr/kvm\nguest.cpu.mode=custom\nguest.cpu.model=Icelake-Server-noTSX\nguest.network.device=br-clguest\nguid=d46e7512-0114-378f-baf5-0c0683092c05\nhost=10.254.0.101,10.254.0.100@roundrobin\nhypervisor.type=kvm\niscsi.session.cleanup.enabled=false\nkeystore.passphrase=****\nlocal.storage.uuid=***\nnetwork.bridge.type=native\npod=1\nport=8250\nprivate.network.device=br-clmgmt\npublic.network.device=br-clpublic\nresource=com.cloud.hypervisor.kvm.resource.LibvirtComputingResource\nvm.migrate.wait=3600\nvxlan.network.vtep.ip=10.1.4.2\nworkers=5\nzone=2\n```\n\nThe agent is selecting 10.1.16.2 address as storage (correct) and private (incorrect, the correct IP should be 10.1.0.2).\n\nThis range is directly routable. The agent can reach the management servers from this address, and the management servers can do stablish new connections with hosts too.\n\nThere is some property that I can change to enforce the private address?\n\n### versions\n\nCloudstack 4.22.1.0\nOS: Rocky Linux 10.2\nAgent: 4.22.1.0\nJava: OpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM (Red_Hat-21.0.11.0.10-1) (build 21.0.11+10-LTS, mixed mode, sharing)\n\n\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\n\n1. Setup a FRR / VXLAN / EVPN enviroment\n2. Setup an advanced network zone in Cloudstack.\n3. Adopt an hypervisor (using the correct ip address on the UI).\n4. Adotion will work and hypervisor will be connected, able to run VMs, but with management IP incorrectly stored.\n\n\n\n### What to do about it?\n\n_No response_","comments":8,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519/comments","created_at":"2026-06-30T23:32:52Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/13519","id":4781110245,"labels":[{"color":"fc2929","default":false,"description":"","id":37843364,"name":"type:bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2NA==","url":"h