t -->\r\n * Feature Idea\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n<!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n-->\r\n~~~\r\nVR\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n<!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n4.20\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n<!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n-->\r\n\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n<!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n-->\r\n\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n<!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly -->\r\n\r\nCurrent VR only resolve its own Guest Network DNS zone record and external records. When two or more peered VPC network, user has to manage the host resolution either by host file or create another forwarder point to VR in upstream DNS. I would say it would be more useful if we populate all DNS record across each peered zone VR with proper domain suffix. So the user do not need to discover new IP changes from peered zone.\r\n\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n<!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below -->\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n<!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files -->\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n<!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? -->\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n<!-- What actually happened? -->\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below -->\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":4,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627/comments","created_at":"2024-02-08T11:54:55Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/8627/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/clouds