N/A otherwise\r\n-->\r\n\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n<!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n-->\r\n\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n<!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly -->\r\n\r\nWhen a Guest Network was created, the port forward and load balancer features only allow to be configure with pre-existing VM in same Guest Network. Sometime user will deploy self managed virtual ip address to support their application such as keepalived, MetalLB..etc. Today, the user will add a secondary NIC to the one of VM instance and then use the assigned NIC ip address to treat the virtual ip setup. Most of the time, it is unavoidable to use this appoarch when LB pool health check limit to L4 port checking. \r\n\r\nI'm wondering if ACS can implement IPAM management abstract under guest network to allow user create IP entities which will able to include into port forwarding or Load balancer member.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n<!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below -->\r\n~~~\r\nN/A\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n<!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files -->\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n<!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? -->\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n<!-- What actually happened? -->\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below -->\r\n~~~\r\nN/A\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":5,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/comments","created_at":"2022-03-25T08:20:22Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163","id":1180482852,"labels":[{"color":"f9d0c4","default":false,"description":"","id":592559219,"name":"component:networking","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking"},{"color":"4471c4","default":false,"description":"","id":1150675549,"name":"type:new-feature","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwNjc1NTQ5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:new-feature"},{"color":"951862","default":false,"description":"","id":2630836378,"name":"status:needs-functional-definition","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjMwODM2Mzc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:needs-functional-definition"},{"color":"E43179","default":false,"description":"","id":6890295339,"name":"status:stale","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABmrGQKw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:stale"},{"color":"ededed","default":false,"id":9849008471,"name":"no-issue-activity","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSwvxVw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/no-issue-activity"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":1302,"created_at":"2021-01-04T09:07:50Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2486961?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DaanHoogland","id":2486961,"login":"DaanHoogland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland"},"html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/19","id":6265435,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels","node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==","number":19,"open_issues":185,"state":"open","title":"unplanned","updated_at":"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M5GXL0k","number":6163,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"Add Support IPAM object to Allow Load Balancer or Port-forward map to floating IP Address","type":{"color":"blue","created_at":"2024-01-25T09:11:09Z","description":"A request, idea, or new functionality","id":93574,"name":"Feature","node_id":"IT_kwDNuP_OAAFthg","updated_at":"2024-10-08T08:30:20Z"},"updated_at":"2026-05-19T02:18:08Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6163","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36956864?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/levindecaro","id":36956864,"login":"levindecaro","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2OTU2ODY0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/levindecaro"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"### problem\n\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" data-sourcepos=\"39:1-43:55;1334-1737\">When creating a CKS Kubernetes cluster and <strong>explicitly selecting a non-default node\ntemplate</strong> (the stock <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">cks-ubuntu-2204-kvm</code> CKS-ready image) in Advanced Settings, the\nnode <strong>Instance</strong> stays in the <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Starting</code> <strong>VM lifecycle state</strong> indefinitely and never\ntransitions to <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Running</code> — even though the libvirt domain is actually up on the KVM host\n(the VNC console is reachable and the guest OS boots).</p>\n\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" data-sourcepos=\"45:1-49:52;1739-2127\">The same cluster creation <strong>succeeds</strong> when the <strong>default SystemVM template</strong>\n(<code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">systemvm-kvm-4.22.0-x86_64</code>) is used for the nodes. The only changed variable between\nthe working and failing cases is the node template selection, which points at the\n<strong>Flexible Kubernetes Clusters per-node template selection path</strong> rather than at\nin-guest provisioning (cloud-init / kubeadm / CNI).</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold\" data-sourcepos=\"55:1-55:22;2375-2396\">STEPS TO REPRODUCE</h2>\n\n<ol class=\"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3\" data-sourcepos=\"57:1-68:24;2398-3079\">\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"57:1-57:37;2398-2434\">ACS 4.22.1.0 on KVM, CKS enabled.</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"58:1-59:21;2435-2538\">Register the stock CKS-ready Ubuntu 22.04 KVM template (<code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">cks-ubuntu-2204-kvm</code>),\nmarked \"For CKS\".</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"60:1-60:57;2539-2595\">Register a supported Kubernetes binaries ISO/version.</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"61:1-63:13;2596-2780\">Create a CloudManaged Kubernetes cluster (3 control node HA) on a <strong>VPC tier</strong> network,\nand in <strong>Advanced Settings explicitly select <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">cks-ubuntu-2204-kvm</code></strong> as the node\ntemplate.</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"64:1-65:27;2781-2886\">Observe the control node Instance in the UI (Instances → the control node):\nit stays in <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Starting</code>.</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"66:1-68:24;2887-3079\">Repeat the exact same cluster creation but <strong>do not select a template</strong> (use the\ndefault <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">systemvm-kvm-4.22.0-x86_64</code>): the node reaches <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Running</code> and the cluster\nprovisions normally.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold\" data-sourcepos=\"70:1-70:20;3081-3100\">EXPECTED RESULTS</h2>\n\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" data-sourcepos=\"72:1-75:11;3102-3367\">Selecting a \"For CKS\" template in Advanced Settings should behave the same as the\ndefault template path: the node Instance transitions <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Starting</code> → <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Running</code> within the\nnormal VM start window, after which CKS provisioning proceeds and the cluster reaches\n<code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Running</code>.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold\" data-sourcepos=\"77:1-77:18;3369-3386\">ACTUAL RESULTS</h2>\n\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" data-sourcepos=\"79:1-79:57;3388-3444\">Behaviour depends solely on the node template selection:</p>\n\n<div class=\"overflow-x-auto w-full px-2 mb-6\" data-sourcepos=\"81:1-85:106;3446-3800\">\n\nPlain Instance deployed from cks-ubuntu-2204-kvm (no CKS) | Reaches Running — works\nCKS node from default SystemVM template systemvm-kvm-4.22.0-x86_64 | Reaches Running, cluster provisions — works\nCKS node from selected cks-ubuntu-2204-kvm template | Instance stuck in Starting indefinitely\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" data-sourcepos=\"87:1-87:21;3802-3822\">In the failing case:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3\" data-sourcepos=\"89:1-95:47;3824-4284\">\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"89:1-90:40;3824-3951\">The control node Instance remains in <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Starting</code> (VM lifecycle state) indefinitely, so\nthe cluster also stays in <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Starting</code>.</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"91:1-92:26;3952-4065\">The libvirt domain is genuinely running on the KVM host: the VNC console is reachable\nand the guest OS boots.</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\" data-sourcepos=\"93:1-95:47;4066-4284\">SSH to the node (port 2222) is not usable; the UI-displayed password is not accepted\non the VNC console (consistent with the node never being marked Running and/or the\nstart/provisioning workflow not completing).</li></ul>\n\n### versions\n\nHypervisor version: KVM Ubuntu 24.04\nACS version: 4.22.1.0\nManagement server: Ubuntu 24.04\n\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\n\n_No response_\n\n### What to do about it?\n\n_No response_","comments":4,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471/comments","created_at":"2026-06-22T23:47:23Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471","id":4721416566,"labels":[{"color":"0db7ed","default":false,"description":"","id":1700119912,"name":"component:kubernetes","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzAwMTE5OTEy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:kubernetes"},{"color":"E95420","default":false,"description":"","id":2051004353,"name":"distro:ubuntu","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDUxMDA0MzUz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/distro:ubuntu"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/13471/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":114,"created_at":"2026-04-13T07:02:43Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12028987?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sureshanaparti","id":12028987,"login":"sureshanaparti","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDI4OTg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sureshanaparti"},"description":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/46","id":15514689,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/46/labels","node_id":"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A7LxB","number":46,"open_issues":252,"