m/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19/labels","node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNjI2NTQzNQ==","number":19,"open_issues":185,"state":"open","title":"unplanned","updated_at":"2026-09-24T11:01:33Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/19"},"node_id":"I_kwDOAJTq2M5VWCmD","number":6861,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack","state":"open","title":"VM Password reset - Unable to set Password Complexity requirement for Special Characters","updated_at":"2026-05-27T02:18:38Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6861","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71042351?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nxsbi","id":71042351,"login":"nxsbi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMDQyMzUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nxsbi"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"<!--\r\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n<!-- Pick one below and delete the rest -->\r\n * Bug Report\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n<!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\n-->\r\n~~~\r\nCompute Cluster UI\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n<!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n4.19.1.1\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n<!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n-->\r\n\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n<!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n-->\r\n\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n<!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly -->\r\n\r\nWe have 2 Compute Clusters:\r\n\r\n- Cluster 1 : Oversubcription = 1\r\n- Cluster 2 : Oversubcription = 2\r\n\r\nRefering to the screenshot below, Cluster 1 is showing the correct No. of CPU Cores allocated. \r\n\r\nBut for Cluster 2, it seems inaccurate. The number of allocation exceeded whats available. Resulting in a UI error. \r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-09-17 at 10 23 55 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/36c46ff6-7d2a-4641-80e5-48e28e040ad0)\r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-09-17 at 10 24 05 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/68972682-4bf4-41d4-8d4e-d61b82132c35)\r\n\r\nBut the bigger problem now, is that both clusters have exceeded the allocation threshold, but there was no notification sent. And neither did cloudstack stop users from creating new virtual machines from the clusters.\r\n\r\nWithout this, Admins would not be able to ensure n+1 sufficient capacity in the event of a node failure. \r\n\r\n![Screenshot 2024-09-17 at 10 34 14 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/550f0ab7-dc3b-4fbf-b757-75153761b17c)\r\n\r\nIn summary, there are 3 Issues:\r\n\r\n- No. Of Allocated CPU Cores should display the full available amount, after oversubscription\r\n- Admin should get Notification if exceeded the global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.notificationthreshold)\r\n- User should not be able to create resources into the cluster after exceeding global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.disablethreshold)\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n<!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below -->\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n<!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files -->\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n<!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? -->\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n- No. Of Allocated CPU Cores should display the full available amount, after oversubscription\r\n- Admin should get Notification if exceeded the global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.notificationthreshold)\r\n- User should not be able to create resources into the cluster after exceeding global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.disablethreshold)\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n<!-- What actually happened? -->\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below -->\r\n~~~\r\n- No. Of Allocated CPU Cores should not displaying total available cores correctly, after oversubscription.\r\n- Admin did not get Notification if exceeded the global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.notificationthreshold)\r\n- User is able to create resources into the cluster after exceeding global setting threshold (cluster.cpu.allocated.capacity.disablethreshold)\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":12,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693/comments","created_at":"2024-09-17T14:38:58Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/9693","id":2531348246,"labels":[{"color":"951862","default":false,"description":"","id":2630836378,"name":"status:needs-functional-definition","nod